`--help` succeeds and documents the full flag set, `--no-lessons` among it.

-- cmd --
booping render-playbook --help
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
usage: booping render-playbook [-h] [--step NAME] [--project PATH]
                               [--output PATH] [--set KEY=VALUE]
                               [--stub-macro DOTTED.PATH=LITERAL]
                               [--no-lessons] [--inline-steps]
                               name

positional arguments:
  name                  Playbook name to render

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --step NAME           Print only this step's body (no surrounding sections)
  --project PATH        Resolve context against this vault instead of the
                        attached project
  --output PATH         Output path (default: stdout); use - for stdout
  --set KEY=VALUE       Override a config value for this render (dotted key,
                        e.g. core.sprint.default_threshold_sp=3); repeatable,
                        later pairs win, and the value wins over every config
                        tier
  --stub-macro DOTTED.PATH=LITERAL
                        Make a macro return LITERAL without executing it (e.g.
                        core.macros.date=19700101-00-00); repeatable, later
                        pairs win
  --no-lessons          Suppress the Lessons section on both the composed and
                        --step surfaces
  --inline-steps        Embed each non-detached step's body in its composed
                        section instead of the fetch command (detached steps
                        keep fetch-form); implied by `inline_steps: true` in
                        the playbook's manifest frontmatter
-- stderr --
